<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wuffingas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century–749</span> · Also known as Wuffings</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wuffingas were the ruling dynasty of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> kingdom of East Anglia from the 6th century until about 749, named after their ancestor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuffa">Wuffa</a>. Its members included Rædwald, probably commemorated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutton-hoo">Sutton Hoo</a>, and King Anna, whose daughters founded monasteries at Ely and elsewhere.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wuffingas.jpg" alt="Wuffingas" width="320" height="282" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Amitchell125 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:East_Anglian_kingdom.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
